# `...N` spreads a list's items; a token is never a list, so spreading one
# would drop it silently. Without a schema too, that is an error.
# error: spread_token.grammar:15:8:
# error: element 1 (IDENT) is a token
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    eof
    err
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser

top! = IDENT IDENT     → (t ...1 2)
